Read CLAUDE.md and the current repo.

Audit the Sprint 0.1 foundation against its specification. Do NOT add
features. For each item below, verify and report PASS/FAIL with file:line
evidence. Fix only FAILs.

1. set_tenant() uses set_config(..., true) — transaction-scoped, not session.
2. Every table has ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY.
3. Every RLS policy uses current_tenant() which returns NULL when unset,
   so missing context yields zero rows (fail closed).
4. TenantTx.WithTenant returns ErrNoTenant when tenant.From fails.
5. AuthMiddleware rejects authenticated users with missing tenant claim
   with 403, not an implicit global grant.
6. AssertNotPrivileged rejects superuser and app_migrator at boot.
7. No handler imports pgxpool directly.
8. Every service in docker-compose.yml has both mem_limit and cpus.
9. tests/tenant_isolation_test.go covers all four required subtests.
10. deploy/initdb/01-roles.sql grants app_user only SELECT on tenants and
    SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on accounts (no DDL).

If any FAIL requires a schema change, produce a new migration rather than
editing 000001. Report at the end: PASS/FAIL table, list of changes made,
and any items you could not verify.